#
# LTP "syscalls" scenario-group skip list (kirk --skip-file).  One test tag per line;
# lines beginning with '#' and blank lines are ignored.  See fs.skip for the
# policy.
#
# The syscalls group is large and many cases are unrelated to a network
# filesystem (IPC, scheduling, namespaces, device nodes, local-fs-only syscalls)
# or require privileges/features NFS does not expose; expect a substantial list
# here.  Seeded from a memfs baseline run; add an entry with a one-line reason.
#
# Baseline (memfs, NFSv4.2): 14609 passed, 411 skipped (TCONF), and 7 fail/broken.
# Of those, cachestat02/ioctl01/remap_file_pages01 were a missing-/dev/shm-and-pts
# guest gap (fixed in init.sh, now pass), leaving these three -- none of which is
# an NFS-server signal:

# Needs an LTP scratch block device (tst_device acquires a loop device + mkfs);
# irrelevant when the fs under test is the NFS mount.  TBROK "Failed to acquire
# device".
fallocate06

# Tests that a core-dumping signal sets the WCOREDUMP bit -- needs core-dump
# capture (core_pattern/ulimit) the minimal guest does not configure; a signal
# test, not a filesystem one.  TFAIL "core dump bit not set".
kill11

# Exercises the mount() syscall's own error paths (mounting via /proc/PID/fd),
# not the NFS filesystem under test.  TFAIL expected-ENOENT.
mount08
